   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the insurance law, in relation to group policies for motor\nvehicles engaged in the business of carrying or transporting passengers\nfor-hire",
    "basePrintNo": "S8437",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8437-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 21,
       "fullName": "Kevin S. Parker",
       "imgName": "416_kevin_s._parker.jpg",
       "incumbent": true,
       "memberId": 416,
       "sessionMemberId": 1194,
       "sessionYear": 2019,
       "shortName": "PARKER"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §3457, Ins L",
    "lawSection": "Insurance Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8437\n\nSPONSOR: LIU\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the insurance law, in relation to group policies for\nmotor vehicles engaged in the business of carrying or transporting\npassengers for-hire\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo authorize the sale of group fleet auto policies for motor vehicles\nengaged in the business of carrying or transporting passengers for-hire.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of the bill would add a new section 3460 to the Insurance\nLaw. This section would:\n\n* Require insurers that issue policies of commercial risk insurance\ninsuring against the losses and liabilities arising out of the ownership\nof a motor vehicle to establish group fleet auto policies and creates a\ndefinition for such policies, which cover motor vehicles engaged in the\nbusiness of transporting passengers for-hire with a seating capacity of\nnot less than eight passengers;\n\n* Provide that group fleet policies may be issued to (1) any person,\nfirm, association, corporation or other entity where the policy insures\nfor-hire vehicles owned by such person, firm, association, corporation\nor other entity or (2) an association that has been in active existence\nfor at least two years, that has been organized for purposes other than\nthat of obtaining insurance and whose members have the same trade or\noccupation, where the policy insures the association's members;\n\n* Require insurers to provide a multiple vehicle reduction to insureds\nbased on the number of motor vehicles that will be covered under such\npolicy and to submit annual reports to the Department of Financial\nServices (DFS) identifying the number of policies eligible for such\ndiscount and the number of policies to which such discount has been\napplied;\n\n* Provide that an association member shall not be deemed to be an\nemployee of such association solely because the member is covered under\nan association's group auto policy;\n\n* Require insurers to make the group auto policies available for sale no\nlater than January 1, 2021; and\n\n* Require DFS to provide for an actuarially appropriate reduction in\ncommercial auto insurance premiums for policies that provide coverage\nfor multiple vehicles.\n\n*Ensures that the language under this bill would not authorize any addi-\ntional increases in premium rates as a result of any one group fleet\npolicy premium rate.\n\nSection two of the bill would provide the effective date. JUSTIFICATION:\n\n\nSection 370 of the Vehicle and Traffic Law requires minimum liability\ncoverages for for-hire vehicles based on carrying capacity. tart III of\nChapter 59 of the Laws of 2019 increased the liability coverage required\nfor for-hire vehicles with a capacity of eight or more persons to a\nminimum of $1.5 million. This has resulted in increases in the rates of\npremiums for this coverage. In order to make this coverage more afforda-\nble, this bill would authorize the sale of group auto policies covering\nfor-hire vehicles with a capacity of eight or more persons and require\ninsurers to provide a multiple vehicle discount to insureds based on the\nnumber of vehicles covered under such policies.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
