  "chapter": 374,
  "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
  "text": "\n \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 67 Chapter 374\n \n        MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 8437, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT to amend the insurance law, in relation to group polices for\n        motor vehicles engaged in the business of carrying or transport-\n        ing passengers for-hire\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This  bill  would  authorize the sale of group fleet auto policies for\nmotor vehicles engaged in  the  business  of  carrying  or  transporting\npassengers for-hire.\n \n  I  fully  support  the  goal  of  this  legislation; however, I do not\nbelieve that the State can or should force an insurer to  provide  group\ninsurance.   Therefore, I have secured an agreement with the Legislature\nto permit, rather than require, an  authorized  insurer  to  offer  such\ngroup  insurance  be  written  on  a  group basis, consistent with other\nsections in Insurance Law Article 34. On the basis of that agreement,  I\nam pleased to sign this bill.\n \n  The bill is approved.                       (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2020
 },
